        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;WHAT THE CODE ACTUALLY DOES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;· No connectivity pre-checks.&lt;/b&gt; Sign-in, registration and reset all make the call and read NO_NETWORK back as a failure reason. Only Google Sign-In tests the network first.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;· An unknown phone number is not its own error.&lt;/b&gt; It resolves to null and is failed exactly like a wrong password, lockout count included — that is the security property, not an oversight.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;· Google goes through the 2FA check too.&lt;/b&gt; Password and Google both end in continueSignedIn(), but Google skips the lockout count.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;· Registration goes straight to Home&lt;/b&gt; — a brand-new account has no authenticator to check.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;· The lockout is checked before the network&lt;/b&gt;, and in fact before submit: it is refreshed as the identifier is typed." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
